<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Sánchez Ramírez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1762">1762</a>–<a href="/years/1811">1811</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Sánchez Ramírez was a Dominican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creole</a> landowner who led the revolt against French rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He defeated General Ferrand at Palo Hincado in November 1808 and, with British naval help, took Santo Domingo in 1809. He returned the colony to Spain and governed it until his death in 1811.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-sanchez-ramirez.jpg" alt="Juan Sánchez Ramírez" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luis Desangles · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_S%C3%A1nchez_Ram%C3%ADrez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Dominican creoles led by <b>Juan Sánchez Ramírez</b> expelled the French from Santo Domingo in 1809, with British help, and voluntarily returned the colony to Spain.</blockquote><a href="/state/espana-boba">España Boba</a></li><li><blockquote>When Napoleon invaded Spain in 1808, Dominican creoles led by <b>Juan Sánchez Ramírez</b> rose in revolt and defeated Ferrand at Palo Hincado in November 1808; Ferrand took his own life.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-santo-domingo">French Santo Domingo</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Captaincy General of Santo Domingo. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/dominican-republic">the Dominican Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=18.46,-69.94&amp;year=1793" aria-label="Santo Domingo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2655 1479 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Juan Sánchez Ramírez"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3105 1749h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3105 1749h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=18.46,-69.94&amp;year=1793">What was here in 1793? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
